{"case_id": "m02", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "12 = 2² × 3  \n18 = 2 × 3²\n\nLCM = 2² × 3² = 4 × 9 = 36\n\n**Answer: 36**", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 4.006, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 457, "output_tokens": 68, "reasoning_tokens": 23, "cost_usd": 5.4e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["GMICloud"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:29:57"}
{"case_id": "m41", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "The general term of an arithmetic sequence is \\(T_n = a + (n-1)d\\), where \\(a\\) is the first term and \\(d\\) the common difference.  \nGiven \\(a = 7\\), \\(d = 4\\), and \\(n = 25\\):  \n\\[\nT_{25} = 7 + (25-1) \\times 4 = 7 + 24 \\times 4 = 7 + 96 = 103.\n\\]  \nTherefore, the 25th term is \\(\\boxed{103}\\).", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.294, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 472, "output_tokens": 333, "reasoning_tokens": 165, "cost_usd": 0.000168, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:01"}
{"case_id": "m42", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "The series is arithmetic with first term \\(a = 3\\) and common difference \\(d = 4\\).\n\nNumber of terms \\(n = 20\\).\n\nSum of first \\(n\\) terms:\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2}\\left[2a + (n-1)d\\right]\n\\]\n\nSubstitute:\n\\[\nS_{20} = \\frac{20}{2}\\left[2(3) + (20-1)(4)\\right] = 10\\left[6 + 19 \\times 4\\right] = 10\\left[6 + 76\\right] = 10 \\times 82\n\\]\n\n\\[\nS_{20} = 820\n\\]\n\n\\boxed{820}", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.265, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 393, "output_tokens": 262, "reasoning_tokens": 63, "cost_usd": 0.000128, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["Parasail"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:01"}
{"case_id": "m05", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "**Simple Interest Calculation**\n\n\\[\n\\text{SI} = P \\times r \\times t\n\\]\n\nWhere:  \n\\( P = \\text{R}5\\,000 \\)  \n\\( r = 8\\% = 0,08 \\)  \n\\( t = 3 \\) years  \n\n\\[\n\\text{SI} = 5\\,000 \\times 0,08 \\times 3\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 5\\,000 \\times 0,24\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\text{R}1\\,200\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** R1 200", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 5.522, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 412, "output_tokens": 232, "reasoning_tokens": 87, "cost_usd": 7.9e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["DeepInfra"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:01"}
{"case_id": "m44", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "\\[\nS_\\infty=\\frac{a}{1-r}\n\\]\n\nHere:\n\n\\[\na=16,\\qquad r=\\frac{8}{16}=\\frac12\n\\]\n\n\\[\nS_\\infty=\\frac{16}{1-\\frac12}\n=\\frac{16}{\\frac12}\n=32\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{32}\n\\]", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.071, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 467, "output_tokens": 157, "reasoning_tokens": 85, "cost_usd": 7.1e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["GMICloud"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:04"}
{"case_id": "m45", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{10} (2k+1) = 2\\sum_{k=1}^{10} k + \\sum_{k=1}^{10} 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 2\\left(\\frac{10 \\times 11}{2}\\right) + 10 = 2 \\times 55 + 10 = 110 + 10 = 120\n\\]\n\nAlternatively, this is an arithmetic series with first term \\(a = 3\\), last term \\(l = 21\\) and \\(n = 10\\):\n\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2}(a + l) = \\frac{10}{2}(3 + 21) = 5 \\times 24 = 120\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{120}\n\\]", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 2.991, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 433, "output_tokens": 375, "reasoning_tokens": 129, "cost_usd": 0.000166, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["Parasail"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:04"}
{"case_id": "m01", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Whole numbers"], "output": "The HCF of 84 and 126 is 42.\n\n**Worked solution:**\n\n1. Prime factorise 84:  \n   \\(84 = 2 \\times 42 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 21 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7\\).\n\n2. Prime factorise 126:  \n   \\(126 = 2 \\times 63 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 21 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 7\\).\n\n3. Identify the common prime factors:  \n   \\(2\\) (lowest power \\(2^1\\)), \\(3\\) (lowest power \\(3^1\\)), \\(7\\) (power \\(7^1\\)).\n\n4. Multiply the common factors:  \n   \\(2 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 42\\).\n\nThus, the highest common factor (HCF) is 42.", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 12.49, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 407, "output_tokens": 456, "reasoning_tokens": 174, "cost_usd": 0.000119, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["DeepInfra"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:06"}
{"case_id": "m43", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Patterns, sequences and series", "grade12"], "output": "**Step 1:** Identify the first term (\\(a\\)) and common ratio (\\(r\\)).  \n\\(a = 2\\)  \n\\(r = \\frac{6}{2} = 3\\)\n\n**Step 2:** Write the formula for the \\(n\\)th term of a geometric sequence.  \n\\(T_n = a r^{n-1}\\)\n\n**Step 3:** Substitute \\(n = 8\\), \\(a = 2\\), \\(r = 3\\).  \n\\(T_8 = 2 \\times 3^{8-1} = 2 \\times 3^7\\)\n\n**Step 4:** Calculate \\(3^7\\).  \n\\(3^7 = 2187\\)\n\n**Step 5:** Multiply.  \n\\(T_8 = 2 \\times 2187 = 4374\\)\n\n**Final answer:**  \n\\(\\boxed{4374}\\)", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 10.076, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 451, "output_tokens": 525, "reasoning_tokens": 220, "cost_usd": 0.000135, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["DeepInfra"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T17:30:11"}
{"case_id": "m16", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Geometry of Straight Lines"], "output": "Let the unknown angle be \\(x\\).\n\nAngles on a straight line sum to \\(180^\\circ\\):\n\\[\nx + 125^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n(angles on a straight line)\n\nSubtract \\(125^\\circ\\) from both sides:\n\\[\nx = 180^\\circ - 125^\\circ = 55^\\circ\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(55^\\circ\\)", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 2.739, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 443, "output_tokens": 170, "reasoning_tokens": 84, "cost_usd": 3.2e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["Baidu"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:01"}
{"case_id": "m11", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Common Fractions"], "output": "\\[\n\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}\n= \\frac{3\\times 3}{4\\times 3}+\\frac{2\\times 4}{3\\times 4}\n= \\frac{9}{12}+\\frac{8}{12}\n= \\frac{17}{12}\n= 1\\frac{5}{12}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1\\frac{5}{12}}\n\\]", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.788, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 537, "output_tokens": 161, "reasoning_tokens": 73, "cost_usd": 7.8e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["GMICloud"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:02"}
{"case_id": "m07", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Exponents"], "output": "\\[\n2^3 \\times 2^2 = 2^{3+2} = 2^5\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2^5 = 32\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** 32", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.789, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 484, "output_tokens": 112, "reasoning_tokens": 69, "cost_usd": 6.4e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["GMICloud"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:02"}
{"case_id": "m13", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 8, "tags": ["Decimal Fractions"], "output": "**Step 1:** Write each decimal as a fraction.  \n\\(0,6 = \\dfrac{6}{10}\\) and \\(0,4 = \\dfrac{4}{10}\\).\n\n**Step 2:** Multiply the fractions.  \n\\(\\dfrac{6}{10} \\times \\dfrac{4}{10} = \\dfrac{6 \\times 4}{10 \\times 10} = \\dfrac{24}{100}\\).\n\n**Step 3:** Convert the fraction back to a decimal.  \n\\(\\dfrac{24}{100} = 0,24\\).\n\n**Final answer:**  \n\\(0,6 \\times 0,4 = 0,24\\).", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 4.521, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 431, "output_tokens": 293, "reasoning_tokens": 153, "cost_usd": 4.1e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["Baidu"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:03"}
{"case_id": "m50", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Exponential and logarithmic functions", "grade12"], "output": "Rewrite in exponential form:  \n\\(\\log_{2} x = 5 \\Rightarrow 2^{5} = x\\)  \n\nTherefore, \\(x = 32\\).  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{32}\n\\]", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 2.139, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 442, "output_tokens": 107, "reasoning_tokens": 61, "cost_usd": 2.7e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["Baidu"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:04"}
{"case_id": "m52", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Functions and inverse functions", "grade12"], "output": "f(x) = 3x - 6  \nLet y = 3x - 6  \nSwap x and y: x = 3y - 6  \nSolve for y: x + 6 = 3y  ⇒  y = \\frac{x+6}{3}  \nTherefore f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x+6}{3}.", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 3.411, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 467, "output_tokens": 381, "reasoning_tokens": 192, "cost_usd": 0.000189, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["Relace"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:05"}
{"case_id": "m54", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Differential calculus", "grade12"], "output": "### Differentiation\n\n\\[\nf(x) = 3x^{4} - 2x^{2} + 5x\n\\]\n\nUsing the power rule \\(\\frac{d}{dx}(ax^{n}) = nax^{n-1}\\) for each term:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(3x^{4}) &= 3 \\times 4x^{4-1} = 12x^{3} \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(-2x^{2}) &= -2 \\times 2x^{2-1} = -4x \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(5x) &= 5 \\times 1x^{1-1} = 5\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\nf'(x) = 12x^{3} - 4x + 5\n\\]", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 5.557, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 395, "output_tokens": 433, "reasoning_tokens": 257, "cost_usd": 5.1e-05, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["Baidu"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:08"}
{"case_id": "m46", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "deepseek__deepseek-v4-flash@low", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "effort": "low", "group": "open", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Finance, growth and decay", "grade12"], "output": "**Solution:**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nP &= \\text{R}20\\,000 \\\\\n\\text{Annual rate} &= 9\\% = 0.09 \\\\\n\\text{Interest per month} &= i = \\frac{0.09}{12} = 0.0075 \\\\\n\\text{Number of periods} &= n = 5 \\times 12 = 60 \\\\\nA &= P(1 + i)^n \\\\\nA &= 20\\,000 (1 + 0.0075)^{60} \\\\\n  &= 20\\,000 (1.0075)^{60} \\\\\n  &= 20\\,000 \\times 1.565681\\ldots \\\\\n  &= 31\\,313.62\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** R31 313,62 (or R31 313.62)", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 25.469, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 407, "output_tokens": 1561, "reasoning_tokens": 958, "cost_usd": 0.000318, "served_models": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"], "hosts": ["DeepInfra"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:07:26"}
